From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:21:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: Put the DE33 planes behind the
 IOMMU

The display engine is master 0 of the H616 IOMMU. Without the iommus
property the DRM DMA device has no IOMMU, so it can only import
physically contiguous buffers, while the video engine (masters 2/3)
produces IOVA-contiguous but physically scattered ones. Describing the
link lets decoded frames be scanned out without a copy.

Taken from the planes node of LibreELEC's "arm64: dts: allwinner: h616:
Add display writeback" (Jernej Skrabec); the writeback node of that
patch is not carried.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 3709c1268..684de3799 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -181,6 +181,7 @@ display_clocks: clock@8000 {
 			planes: planes@100000 {
 				compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-de33-planes";
 				reg = <0x100000 0x180000>;
+				iommus = <&iommu 0>;
 				allwinner,plane-mapping = <&display_clocks>;
 			};
 
